WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Speaker 1: All right, I want to talk about not&nbsp;
one, but two different apparent financial scams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.440
that we've learned about over the last 24 to&nbsp;
48 hours. I've told you now many times it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.640
going to take months, if not years, to learn&nbsp;
the full scope of the grifting and scamming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.080
and and wrongdoing of the former former&nbsp;
administration. And the financial aspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.120
of that are a big piece of it. Let's start with&nbsp;
part one, Donald Trump's presidential salary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.840
We are still learning more and more about&nbsp;
the different lies around Trump's finances.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.720
Donald Trump is reportedly worth about two billion&nbsp;
dollars. I know there are claims that it's like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.320
four or five. The best guesses, he is worth about&nbsp;
two billion dollars. The presidential salary is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.920
about four hundred thousand dollars. OK, we now&nbsp;
have reason to believe that Donald Trump, despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:52.160
promising to donate his presidential salary, that&nbsp;
he did not donate the last six months of salary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.600
about two hundred thousand dollars. Now,&nbsp;
remember, he pledged to donate his full salary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.520
He said, I don't need the money. I'm doing&nbsp;
this for the betterment of the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.040
Yeah. So I'm going to be donating my salary&nbsp;
to federal agencies. There's a new Washington&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.320
Post report which finds that there is no&nbsp;
evidence that Donald Trump actually did that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.360
with a salary for the last six months in office as&nbsp;
president for the first three and a half years of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.160
his presidency, he donated the money to federal&nbsp;
agencies. The Washington Post said it looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.680
it surveyed all major federal agencies and none&nbsp;
of them reported receiving a donation from Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.680
from the point starting in July of twenty twenty&nbsp;
the last six months of his presidency. The paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:39.840
said it was unable to account for that last 200&nbsp;
plus thousand dollars of Trump salary that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.600
supposedly going to be donated. His last known&nbsp;
gift was to the National Park Service in July,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.520
according to government documents. So I think&nbsp;
the explanation for what happened here is very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.920
very simple. We know that as Donald Trump's one&nbsp;
term presidency went on, Trump was more and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.960
agitated about not getting more positive coverage&nbsp;
for the fact that he was donating his salary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:10.640
I think Trump got sick of the fact that he wasn't&nbsp;
getting the coverage he wanted. Trump is both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:18.320
cheap and greedy. So he said if my salary donation&nbsp;
isn't buying me any positive media coverage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.560
I'll just keep the money. That would be very&nbsp;
on brand for Trump. I don't think we have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.760
look very far for a sensible explanation.&nbsp;
Also, by the way, making it extra bizarre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.840
that Trump apparently didn't donate the&nbsp;
last six months of salary is that remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.760
it wasn't I have enough money, so I'm going&nbsp;
to stop making money and do the presidency,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.800
but donate my salary and just make nothing&nbsp;
for these four years. Trump kept making money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.320
while he was president. He reportedly made one&nbsp;
point six billion dollars over those four years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.920
meaning that even the salary he donated is&nbsp;
like zero point one percent of what he made.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.840
And he still apparently didn't donate the full&nbsp;
salary despite his promise. Now, I think it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.520
important to mention, just to be thorough,&nbsp;
The Washington Post clarified, we were unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.840
to verify Trump's donations and we did not&nbsp;
get a response when we asked for comment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.280
It's theoretically possible that he donated it&nbsp;
somewhere and we don't know where and we just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.960
can't track it down. It's possible. But again, the&nbsp;
point is he had been doing it to federal agencies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.600
reporting it. There were disclosures. There was&nbsp;
documentation. The paper trail stops with six&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.400
months left to go. The paper went to Trump's&nbsp;
business and asked about it. They went to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:41.120
lawyer who the former lawyer who helped arrange&nbsp;
the donations. Nobody responded. OK, now, also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.560
some may not know. Trump continues to receive a&nbsp;
pension of two hundred and twenty thousand dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.480
a year as a former president as well. So there&nbsp;
are people who wrote to me and said, David, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.040
is a sign that Trump is broke. I actually doubt&nbsp;
it that that would make keeping the money more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.880
logical. Certainly if Trump was broke, it would&nbsp;
make sense to keep that last two hundred thousand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.680
Trump's not likely broke, and that's what&nbsp;
actually makes the story even wackier. It's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:13.520
you know, Trump, the fact that he is so cheap&nbsp;
despite being a billionaire is actually even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.440
stunning than Trump somehow ending up broke.&nbsp;
But no, he made one point six billion during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.600
his four years in the White House. I don't think&nbsp;
he's broke, but there is an even bigger scam. OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:30.000
and we're going to talk about this in a moment.&nbsp;
Donald Trump has now raised somewhere between 70&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.480
and 80 million dollars from his followers on the&nbsp;
promise that the money was going to be used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:43.040
fight the election results, to fund audits,&nbsp;
to to fund recounts, to fund lawsuits and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:48.720
investigations, to try to overturn the election&nbsp;
and put Trump back in power. The latest report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:55.840
is that none of the money, the 70 or 75 or 80&nbsp;
or 82 million that was donated for that reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:01.520
none of it actually was used by. Trump&nbsp;
for the things he claimed he was raising,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.400
raising the money for, and of course, on the tail&nbsp;
end of it, his supporters won't actually care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.840
He could walk up to one of them&nbsp;
on Fifth Avenue and shoot them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:15.200
and they would cheer and assume that it&nbsp;
was secretly antifa or something like that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:22.480
And what I want to talk about next is a new report&nbsp;
that not only did Donald Trump not use the 70 or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.800
80 million for what he said he was going to use&nbsp;
it for, there are new disclosures which show that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:36.000
Donald Trump funneled those donations into his&nbsp;
personal businesses. Let's talk about that next.

